Add `vasm=<string>` option to -vasm compiler switch

The existing use of `vasm` will print a disassembly of all functions
being compiled. This can result in an unmanageably large amount of output.
The addition of `=<string> enables specification of a pattern (a
simple string) that is matched against a function's mangled name.
If it is a match, it is disassembled and displayed.
